<a id="a594358a29d9f8e40d0da8b3fa1b7c5a1" name="a594358a29d9f8e40d0da8b3fa1b7c5a1"></a>
<h2 class="memtitle"><span class="permalink"><a href="#a594358a29d9f8e40d0da8b3fa1b7c5a1">&#9670;&#160;</a></span>cancel()</h2>

<div class="memitem">
<div class="memproto">
      <table class="memname">
        <tr>
          <td class="memname">void AsyncTask::cancel </td>
          <td>(</td>
          <td class="paramname"><span class="paramname"><em></em></span></td><td>)</td>
          <td></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
</div><div class="memdoc">

<p>notify the task that it should be cancelled. </p>
<p>N.B.: Cancelling is also asynchronous, the task will not be cancelled immediately. If the task is cancelled in the middle of an operation (i.e. purging 1000 keygroups), the Engine is left in an indeterminate state and this is the script's responsibility to restore a valid state. </p>

